weakness|limitation|NOUN|fault or area needing improvement|A fault or limitation that makes a person or thing less effective.|điểm yếu; hạn chế|The review identified a weakness in the booking process.|Bản đánh giá chỉ ra một điểm yếu trong quy trình đặt chỗ.|Countable for a particular limitation; weakness in names the affected area.|0
weakness|lack-strength|NOUN|lack of physical or other strength|The state of having little strength or power.|sự yếu đi; tình trạng yếu sức|After the long journey, he felt weakness in his legs.|Sau chuyến đi dài, anh ấy cảm thấy chân yếu đi.|Usually uncountable for the condition; distinct from a countable fault in a plan.|1
chin|lower-face|NOUN|part of the face below the mouth|The part of the face that projects below the lower lip.|cằm|She rested her chin on her hand while reading.|Cô ấy tựa cằm lên tay trong lúc đọc sách.|Countable; under one's chin identifies a position beneath this part of the face.|-
grapefruit|citrus-fruit|NOUN|large tart citrus fruit|A large round citrus fruit with juicy flesh that often tastes tart and slightly bitter.|bưởi chùm|He cut a grapefruit in half and placed it in a small bowl.|Anh ấy bổ đôi một quả bưởi chùm rồi đặt vào một chiếc bát nhỏ.|Countable for a whole fruit; uncountable for its flesh as food. Grapefruit is distinct from the larger pomelo.|-
middle|central-part|NOUN|central part or position|The central part or position between the ends or sides of something.|phần giữa; vị trí giữa|A low table stood in the middle of the room.|Một chiếc bàn thấp đặt ở giữa phòng.|Often the middle of something; in the middle locates something centrally or within a sequence.|0
middle|central-adjective|ADJECTIVE|between outer or end parts|Situated between the outer parts or between the beginning and end.|ở giữa; thuộc phần giữa|The middle shelf holds the books we use most often.|Kệ ở giữa đựng những cuốn sách chúng tôi dùng thường xuyên nhất.|Usually before a noun; middle identifies relative position rather than an exact numerical midpoint.|1
port|ship-harbour|NOUN|place where ships load and unload|A place by the sea or another navigable waterway where ships stop to load or unload.|cảng; bến cảng|The ship reached the port shortly before dawn.|Con tàu đến cảng ngay trước bình minh.|Countable for a harbour or town; in port and leave port often omit an article.|0
